// ============================================================
//  Module / Group definition
// ============================================================

/**
 * @defgroup FcsFastSim FCS Fast Simulator
 * @ingroup  StFcsFastSimulatorMaker
 *
 * @brief Fast Monte-Carlo digitizer for the STAR Forward Calorimeter System (FCS).
 *
 * @section fcs_overview FCS Overview
 *
 * The **Forward Calorimeter System (FCS)** is a sampling calorimeter installed
 * in the STAR detector at BNL to extend the pseudorapidity coverage to the
 * forward region (approximately 2.5 < η < 4.0).  It consists of three
 * sub-detector layers arranged longitudinally along the beam axis:
 *
 * | Index (ehp) | Name | Acronym | Technology | Detector IDs |
 * |:-----------:|------|---------|-----------|:------------:|
 * | 0 | Electromagnetic Calorimeter | ECAL | W-Shashlyk (lead/scintillator) | 0 (North), 1 (South) |
 * | 1 | Hadronic Calorimeter | HCAL | Iron/scintillator | 2 (North), 3 (South) |
 * | 2 | Pre-shower Detector | PRES | EPD tiles | 4 (North), 5 (South) |
 *
 * Each sub-detector is split into two halves (**North**, ns = 0; **South**, ns = 1)
 * that together surround the beam pipe.
 *
 * ### ECAL geometry
 * - 22 columns × 34 rows per side → **748 channels** per side
 * - Tungsten-Shashlyk (W-Shashlyk) sampling calorimeter
 * - Read out via wavelength-shifting (WLS) fibres
 *
 * ### HCAL geometry
 * - 13 columns × 20 rows per side → **260 channels** per side
 * - Iron absorber / scintillator tiles
 * - Light transported through WLS fibres; lateral light leakage is a
 *   configurable effect (see @ref fcs_leaky_hcal)
 *
 * ### PRES geometry
 * - 16 columns × 12 rows per side → **192 channels** per side
 * - Re-uses the Event Plane Detector (EPD) scintillator tiles placed in
 *   front of the ECAL as a preshower layer
 * - Read out via the same DEP (Detector Electronics Package) readout as
 *   ECAL/HCAL
 *
 * @section fcs_simulation Simulation Chain
 *
 * The fast simulator bypasses full pulse-shape simulation.  For each
 * sub-event it performs the following steps:
 *
 * -# **GEANT hit ingestion** – reads three GEANT-3 hit tables produced by
 *    the full GEANT simulation step:
 *    - `g2t_wca_hit` (ECAL) via `St_g2t_emc_hit`
 *    - `g2t_hca_hit` (HCAL) via `St_g2t_hca_hit`
 *    - `g2t_epd_hit` (PRES) via `St_g2t_epd_hit`
 *
 * -# **Channel accumulation** – energy deposits from multiple GEANT sub-hits
 *    in the same physical cell are summed into a single `StFcsHit`.
 *    Look-up maps (`mEcalMap`, `mHcalMap`, `mPresMap`) provide O(1) access to
 *    already-created hits indexed by `[ns][id]`.
 *
 * -# **Digitisation** – the accumulated deposited energy `de` is converted to
 *    an ADC count via:
 *    @f[
 *      \mathrm{ADC} = \left\lfloor \frac{de}{SF \times G \times C} \right\rfloor
 *    @f]
 *    where:
 *    - @f$SF@f$ = sampling fraction (from `StFcsDb::getSamplingFraction`)
 *    - @f$G@f$ = channel gain (from `StFcsDb::getGain`)
 *    - @f$C@f$ = gain correction (from `StFcsDb::getGainCorrection`)
 *    The result is capped at **32 760** (= 4095 × 8, i.e. 12-bit ADC × 8
 *    time-bin sum).
 *
 * -# **Zero suppression** – hits whose ADC value does not exceed the
 *    per-detector threshold from `StFcsDb::getZeroSuppression` are discarded.
 *
 * -# **Energy reconstruction** – the surviving hits have their energy set to
 *    the *digitised* value:
 *    @f[
 *      E_{\mathrm{digi}} = \mathrm{ADC} \times G \times C
 *    @f]
 *    This matches what the full readout chain (`StFcsRawHitMaker`) would
 *    produce from real ADC data.
 *
 * -# **StEvent population** – surviving hits are inserted into the
 *    `StFcsCollection` inside the current `StEvent`.
 *
 * @section fcs_leaky_hcal HCAL Light-Collection Models
 *
 * The `FcsLeakyHcal` attribute (set via `StFcsFastSimulatorMaker::setLeakyHcal`)
 * selects among four models of WLS-fibre light collection in the HCAL:
 *
 * | Value | Description |
 * |:-----:|-------------|
 * | 0 | Straight Birk's-law quenching; uses `g2t_hca_hit_st::de` |
 * | 1 | Leaky HCAL: light from one physical tower is distributed among up to four adjacent WLS-fibre channels (`deA`–`deD`) |
 * | 2 | 2-D (x–y) light-collection efficiency, single-side readout (not leaky) |
 * | 3 | 2-D light-collection efficiency, double-side readout (leaky) |
 *
 * In leaky mode (1 or 3) the simulator looks up the column number of the
 * hit tower and distributes light to `id + jj` for `jj ∈ {-2, -1, 0, +1}`,
 * with boundary clamping at column 1 and the last column.
 *
 * @section fcs_zdep_eff HCAL Z-Dependent Efficiency
 *
 * The `FcsHcalZDepEff` attribute (set via
 * `StFcsFastSimulatorMaker::setHcalZDepEff`) selects the longitudinal (z)
 * light-collection efficiency profile:
 *
 * | Value | Description |
 * |:-----:|-------------|
 * | 0 | Straight Birk — uses raw `de` |
 * | 1 | "Normal" profile — uses `deA` field |
 * | 2 | "Bad" profile — uses `deB` field |
 *
 * @section fcs_epd_mapping EPD → PRES Mapping
 *
 * The PRES sub-detector physically uses EPD tiles, so its GEANT hits come
 * from the `g2t_epd_hit` table.  The EPD `volume_id` encodes:
 * @code
 *   ew  = volume_id / 100000          // 1 = West, 2 = East
 *   pp  = (volume_id % 100000) / 1000 // super-sector number (1–12)
 *   tt  = (volume_id % 1000)   / 10   // tile number within super-sector
 * @endcode
 * Only the **east** side (`ew != 1`) is mapped to FCS PRES; the west side is
 * skipped.  A known XML-ordering bug requires swapping even/odd tile indices
 * for `tt > 1`; this is handled inline (see comment "Hack! reverse TT
 * Even/Odd").  The deposited energy is scaled by **1000** to convert from the
 * EPD units (GeV) to the PRES units (MeV-scale tile signals).
 *
 * @{
 */

// ============================================================
//  Class documentation
// ============================================================

/**
 * @class StFcsFastSimulatorMaker
 * @brief STAR Maker that converts GEANT hits into digitised FCS hits in StEvent.
 *
 * `StFcsFastSimulatorMaker` is a concrete `StMaker` that sits inside the BFC
 * (Barrel and Forward Chain) reconstruction chain.  It is instantiated once
 * per job and is called once per event via the standard `Make()` interface.
 *
 * ### Responsibilities
 * - Fetch `g2t_wca_hit`, `g2t_hca_hit`, and `g2t_epd_hit` tables from the
 *   data store.
 * - Accumulate energy deposits per FCS channel.
 * - Digitise energies using calibration constants from `StFcsDb`.
 * - Apply zero suppression.
 * - Populate `StFcsCollection` inside `StEvent` with `StFcsHit` objects.
 *
 * ### Dependencies
 * | Component | Role |
 * |-----------|------|
 * | `StFcsDb` | Calibration constants (gain, sampling fraction, zero suppression, channel mapping) |
 * | `StEvent` / `StFcsCollection` | Output container |
 * | `g2t_emc_hit`, `g2t_hca_hit`, `g2t_epd_hit` tables | GEANT hit input |
 *
 * ### Typical usage (BFC / ROOT macro)
 * @code{.cpp}
 * StFcsFastSimulatorMaker* fcsSim = new StFcsFastSimulatorMaker("fcsSim");
 * fcsSim->setLeakyHcal(0);      // straight Birk (default)
 * fcsSim->setHcalZDepEff(0);    // no z-dependent efficiency (default)
 * @endcode
 *
 * @see StFcsDb, StFcsHit, StFcsCollection
 */

// ============================================================
//  Constructor / Destructor
// ============================================================

/**
 * @fn StFcsFastSimulatorMaker::StFcsFastSimulatorMaker(const char* name)
 * @brief Construct the maker and initialise light-collection attributes to
 *        their defaults (straight Birk, no z-dependent efficiency).
 *
 * @param name  Maker name used by the `StMaker` chain framework.
 *              Defaults to `"fcsSim"`.
 */

/**
 * @fn StFcsFastSimulatorMaker::~StFcsFastSimulatorMaker()
 * @brief Default destructor.  No heap memory is owned by the maker itself;
 *        hit objects are owned by `StFcsCollection` after `fillStEvent`.
 */

// ============================================================
//  Public interface
// ============================================================

/**
 * @fn int StFcsFastSimulatorMaker::Init()
 * @brief Initialise the maker: retrieve `StFcsDb` and zero the hit maps.
 *
 * Called once by the framework before the first event.  Looks up the
 * `"fcsDb"` dataset in the data store; if it is absent the method logs an
 * error and returns `kStErr`.  On success it clears `mEcalMap`, `mHcalMap`,
 * and `mPresMap` to `nullptr` and returns `kStOK`.
 *
 * @return `kStOK` on success, `kStErr` if `StFcsDb` is not found.
 */

/**
 * @fn void StFcsFastSimulatorMaker::Clear(Option_t *option)
 * @brief Reset per-event state: zero all channel hit-pointer maps.
 *
 * Called by the framework at the start (or end) of each event to prepare
 * the maker for a new event.  Clears `mEcalMap`, `mHcalMap`, and `mPresMap`
 * to `nullptr` and delegates to `StMaker::Clear`.
 *
 * @param option  Forwarded to `StMaker::Clear`; typically `""`.
 */

/**
 * @fn int StFcsFastSimulatorMaker::Make()
 * @brief Main per-event entry point: create or retrieve `StEvent` and
 *        `StFcsCollection`, then delegate to `fillStEvent`.
 *
 * If no `StEvent` exists in the data store a new one is created and added.
 * If the event has no `StFcsCollection` a new one is created and attached.
 * `fillStEvent` then performs all GEANT-hit ingestion, digitisation, and
 * zero suppression.
 *
 * @return `kStOk` unconditionally (errors inside `fillStEvent` are logged but
 *         do not abort the event).
 */

/**
 * @fn void StFcsFastSimulatorMaker::setDebug(int v)
 * @brief Enable or adjust the debug-message verbosity level.
 *
 * Thin wrapper around `StMaker::SetDebug` provided for backward
 * compatibility with older macro scripts.
 *
 * @param v  Debug level.  0 = silent, 1 = per-hit INFO messages,
 *           2 = additionally calls `StFcsCollection::print()`.
 *           Defaults to 1.
 */

/**
 * @fn void StFcsFastSimulatorMaker::setLeakyHcal(int v)
 * @brief Select the HCAL lateral light-collection model.
 *
 * Stores the value as the maker attribute `"FcsLeakyHcal"` (read during
 * `fillStEvent` via `IAttr`).
 *
 * | v | Model |
 * |:-:|-------|
 * | 0 | Straight Birk — uses `g2t_hca_hit_st::de` (default) |
 * | 1 | Leaky HCAL — distributes light to ≤ 4 neighbouring WLS channels (`deA`–`deD`) |
 * | 2 | 2-D xy light-collection efficiency, single-side (not leaky) |
 * | 3 | 2-D xy light-collection efficiency, double-side (leaky) |
 *
 * @param v  Light-collection model index (0–3).  Defaults to 1.
 */

/**
 * @fn void StFcsFastSimulatorMaker::setHcalZDepEff(int v)
 * @brief Select the HCAL longitudinal (z) light-collection efficiency profile.
 *
 * Stores the value as the maker attribute `"FcsHcalZDepEff"` (read during
 * `fillStEvent` via `IAttr`).
 *
 * | v | Profile |
 * |:-:|---------|
 * | 0 | Straight Birk, no z correction (default) |
 * | 1 | "Normal" z-dependent profile (uses `deA` field) |
 * | 2 | "Bad" z-dependent profile (uses `deB` field) |
 *
 * @param v  Profile index (0–2).  Defaults to 1.
 */

// ============================================================
//  Private implementation
// ============================================================

/**
 * @fn void StFcsFastSimulatorMaker::fillStEvent(StEvent* event)
 * @brief Core implementation: ingest GEANT hits, digitise, zero-suppress,
 *        and populate `StFcsCollection`.
 *
 * This method performs the complete simulation pipeline for one event.
 * It is broken into three GEANT-table reading blocks followed by a single
 * digitisation/zero-suppression loop.
 *
 * #### Step 1 – ECAL (`g2t_wca_hit`)
 * Iterates over rows of `g2t_emc_hit_st`.  For each hit, `volume_id` is
 * decoded as:
 * @code
 *   ns = volume_id / 1000 - 1   // 0 = North, 1 = South
 *   id = volume_id % 1000 - 1   // channel id within sub-detector
 * @endcode
 * A new `StFcsHit` is created on first encounter; subsequent hits to the
 * same cell add their `de` to the existing object.  The GEANT track pointer
 * and energy are recorded via `StFcsHit::addGeantTrack`.
 *
 * #### Step 2 – HCAL (`g2t_hca_hit`)
 * Identical volume-id decoding.  The selected `leakyHcal` model controls
 * which `de` field(s) from `g2t_hca_hit_st` are used and whether energy is
 * distributed to neighbouring channels (leaky modes 1 and 3).  In leaky
 * mode the loop index `j ∈ {0,1,2,3}` maps to column offsets
 * `jj ∈ {-2,-1,0,+1}` with boundary clamping.
 *
 * #### Step 3 – PRES (`g2t_epd_hit`)
 * Decodes EPD `volume_id`, skips the west side (`ew == 1`), applies the
 * even/odd tile swap, converts EPD coordinates via
 * `StFcsDb::getIdfromEPD(pp, tt, det, id)`, scales energy by 1000.
 *
 * #### Step 4 – Digitisation and zero suppression
 * For every hit in the temporary `hits` vector:
 * -# Compute `ADC = int(de / (SF × G × C))`, capped at 4095 × 8 = 32760.
 * -# If `ADC > ZS` threshold: set `adc` slot 0 and digitised energy on the
 *    hit, add to `StFcsCollection`.
 * -# Otherwise: `delete` the hit.
 *
 * @param event  Pointer to the current `StEvent` (must not be `nullptr`).
 */

/** @} */ // end of FcsFastSim group
